description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/learning-signal-health-observer.ts, stop the observer reporting "healthy" from a sample that was selected by the very quantity it measures.

It fetches /concepts/search with no query, which orders by relevance DESC, and relevance is (times_succeeded + 1) / (times_loaded + 2). So when the page fills to its limit it returns precisely the concepts that HAVE successes. Measured 2026-09-10: it reported total_concepts 5000, loaded_concepts 5000, loaded_with_success 5000, success_credit_ratio 1 and diagnosis "healthy", while the store held 69,142 concepts with a true ratio of 0.456 and the compose_lesson subgroup at 17 loaded / 0 ever succeeded. A saturated page cannot support a health verdict at any volume, so the observer must abstain and say why.

Make exactly three edits. Each anchor below occurs exactly once in the file; copy it verbatim.

EDIT 1 - replace this line:
  const subgroupSuccessCreditRatios = {}; // to hold ratios per source_type
with:
  // THE SAMPLE IS SELECTED BY THE QUANTITY BEING MEASURED. /concepts/search with no query
  // orders by relevance DESC, and relevance is (times_succeeded + 1) / (times_loaded + 2),
  // so a page that fills to its limit returns precisely the concepts that HAVE successes.
  // Measured 2026-09-10: total = loaded = loadedWithSuccess = 5000 against a store of 69,142
  // concepts whose true ratio was 0.456 - the numerator had chosen the denominator.
  const pageLimit = Number(new URL(searchUrl).searchParams.get("limit") ?? 0);
  const sampleSaturated = pageLimit > 0 && total >= pageLimit;

(The removed line was a dead declaration: it was never populated and never read.)

EDIT 2 - replace this line:
  const enoughVolume = loaded.length >= minLoadedVolume;
with:
  const enoughVolume = loaded.length >= minLoadedVolume && !sampleSaturated;

EDIT 3 - replace this line:
        : (enoughVolume ? "healthy" : "insufficient load volume to judge (cold start)"),
with:
        : (enoughVolume
            ? "healthy"
            : sampleSaturated
              ? `unrepresentative sample: the search page filled to its limit of ${pageLimit} and is ordered by relevance, which is derived from the success counts this check measures, so no health verdict can be drawn from it`
              : "insufficient load volume to judge (cold start)"),

Do not change anything else. Do not alter emitGap, the ConceptLike interface, the fetch call, or the ratio arithmetic. The file must typecheck; searchUrl and total are both already in scope at the point of EDIT 1.

